# 0.0.6 to 0.0.10, from the "Changes in" sections of README.md at the tag:
#   0.0.7  `Worker.new bindings` is checked at the first event, not at load. No
#          API change.
#   0.0.8  smaller `roc_event` code. No API change.
#   0.0.9  allocator size classes, the makeHandler options `stats` and `trace`.
#          No Roc API change.
#   0.0.10 roc-cbor 0.2.3 to 0.5.0 in the platform header, with strict reads.
#          For app authors: data that Roc stores (cells, attachments, Memo)
#          reads strictly and keeps `Err(Null)`; values from JS (RPC, queues,
#          Ai.run!) still read a `null` field as no key; a bare `List(U8)` SQL
#          parameter is `BadParam` (`Sql.blob` now gives `Sql.Blob`); a
#          `List(U8)` writes a byte string; `Queue.json` and KV metadata write
#          big integers and bytes as text and read them back; `Cbor.State` is
#          `Cbor.Reader`, and a custom `encoder_for` takes `Cbor.Writer`; new
#          `Object.Cell.migrate!`, `Object.Attachment.migrate!`,
#          `Queue.legacy_0_2`, `Kv.Metadata.parse_legacy`, `Cbor.parse_legacy`
#          for data of 0.0.9; a `--opt=dev` build needs
#          `--wasm-stack-size=2097152`.
# The overview and the topics (objects, queues, rpc, websockets, d1, worker)
# were changed for these. The run-time rules (null handling, BadParam, the text
# forms of Queue.json) are taken from MODULES.md 1 and README.md at the tag, the
# platform's own record of its checks; this repin compiled every program but ran
# none. cfw_objects compiles a `migrate!` call.

